From ce134b9fc399c0b99b1c0f40c4bb4474cb380a26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:46:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/17] ASoC: codecs: add Cirrus Logic CS42L81 (Apple) driver

The CS42L81 has no public datasheet. The control protocol and the
playback sequences were reconstructed from iOS 16.7.10's
AppleCS42L81Audio/AppleCSSPIv2Audio:

 - SPI framing: write 6C page reg 00 val, read 6D page reg 00 xx with
   the value in the 5th byte; device ID 42 A8 1x at 0x01..0x03.
 - Power up (enableAudio), sample-rate programming, the ASP slot map
   with the codec as BCLK/LRCK provider, the speaker-only routing state,
   the speaker volume (CS35L33-style 0.5 dB code, +0x34 offset) and the
   power down with a bounded PDN_DONE poll.

Only the speaker playback path is implemented. Register names are
descriptive guesses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig   |   8 +
 sound/soc/codecs/Makefile  |   2 +
 sound/soc/codecs/cs42l81.c | 722 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 732 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/codecs/cs42l81.c

